{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And all its pegs.</b> At the time of erecting the Mishkan they would tie these pegs with cords to the edges of the curtains around — south, west, and north — and pull the cords with force and drive the pegs into the ground, so that the curtains would be stretched taut, in order that they not sag and fall into the Mishkan because of their weight, diminishing its interior space. Even though there is no proof for this matter, there is an allusion to it: ״אהל בל יצען ובל יסע יתדותיו לנצח״ (a tent that shall not be taken down and whose pegs shall never be uprooted). End of the section of Terumah."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:44.520001139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}